{"name":"Cranberry Red","hex":"#7e5350","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cranberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shrub belonging to the section Vaccinium sect. Oxycoccus of the genus Vaccinium.","The edible red berry of that shrub."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of the intense red colour of a cranberry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cranberry"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cranberry","blocks":[{"text":"Cranberries are a group of evergreen dwarf shrubs or trailing vines in the subgenus Oxycoccus of the genus Vaccinium. Cranberries are low, creeping shrubs or vines up to 2 meters (7 ft) long and 5 to 20 centimeters in height; they have slender stems that are not thickly woody and have small evergreen leaves. The flowers are dark pink. The fruit is a berry that is larger than the leaves of the plant; it is initially light green, turning red when ripe. The raw berry is edible and has a tart taste due to the low sugar content and high acidity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Cranberry_bog.jpg/330px-Cranberry_bog.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cranberry"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a 